  "Convert rights declarations into a workable licensing market instead of a binary open/closed web.": "Soppi dëklaraasion sañ-sañ ba doon marse bu lisaans bu man a doxal, du rekk web bu «ubbeeku/tëj» rekk.",
  "Copied ✓": "Copié ✓",
  "Copy": "Copie",
  "Correct positioning: independent research drafts, protocol proposals, and an open specification experiment.": "Barab bu jub: brouyon yu njàngat yu bawoo ci boppam, digal yu protokol, ak eksperimaŋ bu spesifikasyon bu ubbeeku.",
  "Corrected an earlier default: Belgium (BE) now maps to Dutch instead of French — Flemish speakers are the country’s majority (~60%) over Walloon French speakers (~40%).": "Ñu jubal njëlbeen bu njëkk: Belsig (BE) léegi dafay dëppook Holandé, du Faranse — waxkat yu Flamand ñoo ëpp ci réew mi (~60%) ci kaw waxkat yu Faranse bu Wallon (~40%).",
  "Corrected an earlier default: Kazakhstan (KZ) now maps to Kazakh instead of Russian, now that a Kazakh translation exists — the same kind of fix as the earlier Belgium correction.": "Ñu jubal njëlbeen bu njëkk: Kazakstan (KZ) léegi dafay dëppook Kazak, du Rus, ndax léegi am na tekki bu Kazak — mel ni jubal googu njëkk bu Belsig.",
  "Could AI Be Conscious?": "Could AI Be Conscious?",
  "Crawler access rules": "Yoonu Jokkoo bu Crawler",
  "Crawler simulator": "Simulateur bu Crawler",
  "Currency": "Xaalis",
  "Custom tier": "Xët-xët bu Sa Bopp",
  "Daily Nous reports on a retracted Journal of Medical Ethics submission containing multiple fabricated, AI-hallucinated references — complete with fake university affiliations and defunct email addresses — that the author reportedly left uncorrected even after being given a chance to fix proofs. The piece contrasts this with Bioethics, whose automated reference-checking would have caught the problem, and argues the real bottleneck isn't detection technology (one commenter's script flagged the fake citations in under a minute) but unpaid reviewer labor and publishing incentives that reward throughput over scrutiny.": "Daily Nous dafay wax ci benn xët bu ñu génn ci Journal of Medical Ethics, bu ñu bàyyi ci sabab bu am reference yu AI sos, yu ñàkk am dëgg — ak affiliation yu université yu ñàkk am dëgg ak imel yu tëj — bu bindkat bi ñu koy wax, jubalu ko, li mu jekk ba ñu ko jox sañu jubal ay proof. Xët bi dafay men lii ak Bioethics, mu ñu am odit-reference bu automatik moo dina xam problem bi, te dafa wax ne mbir mu ëpp njariñ moo di teknoloji bu xam-xam bu néew (script bu benn commentateur wone na citation yu ñàkk dëgg ci suuf benn minute), waaye moo di liggéey bu reviewer yu ñu feywul ak ndigal yu publication yu ñu di jox njariñ ci lu bare, du ci wérgu-wér.",
  "Data free-riding vs. trillion-dollar AI valuations": "Jël Done bu Fey Wuñu ci Boppu ci Njëg AI bu Tollu ci Trillion",
  "DeepMind CEO calls for an independent standards body to regulate frontier AI": "DeepMind CEO calls for an independent standards body to regulate frontier AI",
  "Demis Hassabis proposed a FINRA-style regulator for frontier model releases: labs would submit models for review up to 30 days before deployment, voluntary at first, with a path toward mandatory compliance in the US market.": "Demis Hassabis dafa digël benn régulator bu mel ni FINRA ngir génne modèl yu jiitu: laboratoire yi dinañu yóbbu modèl yi ngir seetlu ba fukki fan ak juróom (30 fan) laata ñu génne leen, ci njëkk ci anam bu bawoo ci boppam, waaye am na yoon jëm ci conformite bu war ci marse Amerik.",
  "Denied": "Bañ",
  "Deployable policy starter template": "Modèl bu Politig bu Ñu Man a Jëfandiku",
  "Deployable policy starter template at /downloads/agiright-policy-starter.zip — a minimal static site with the full machine-readable layer, ready for Cloudflare Pages or any static host.": "Modèl bu politig bu ñu man a jëfandiku ci /downloads/agiright-policy-starter.zip — sit statik bu suufe bu am wàllu masin man a jàng bu mat sepp, deŋkal ngir Cloudflare Pages walla béy hosting statik bu nekk.",
  "Deploying machine-readable policies on your site": "Def politig bu masin man a jàng ci sa sit",
  "Disclaimer": "Disclaimer",
  "Distinct from human UI, SEO, or plain APIs, the AI Ingestion & Capability Layer gives websites a machine-facing architecture: a Manifest Layer (entry points like /llms.txt and /ai/manifest.json), a Corpus Layer (machine-readable knowledge), a Capability Layer (agent-callable tools), and a Governance Layer (provenance, licensing, versioning). Static-first, upgradeable toward APIs and MCP. Note: in this paper AICL names the ingestion architecture; on this site's protocol pages AICL refers to the AI Content Licensing Layer.": "Wute ci UI bu nit, SEO, walla API bu yomb, wàllu AI Ingestion & Capability Layer dafay jox sit internet yi arsik bu jëm ci masin: wàllu Manifest (dugub ni /llms.txt ak /ai/manifest.json), wàllu Corpus (xam-xam bu masin man a jàng), wàllu Kapasite (jumtukaay yu agent man a woo), ak wàllu Gouvernans (fu li bawoo, lisaans, version). Statik ci njëkk, waaye man a yokk ba ci API ak MCP. Nota: ci xët bii AICL day tudde arsik bu ingestion; ci xët yu protokol yu sit bii AICL dafay tuddoo Wàllu Lisaansu Content AI.",
  "Do Large Language Models Possess a Theory of Mind? A Comparative Evaluation Using the Strange Stories Paradigm": "Do Large Language Models Possess a Theory of Mind? A Comparative Evaluation Using the Strange Stories Paradigm",
  "Docs": "Dokimaa",
  "Docs / Examples": "Dokimaa / Misaal",
  "Document library": "Bibliotek bu Dokimaa",
  "Does AI have rights — and which framings are even coherent?": "Ndax AI am na sañ-sañ — te ban anam-xalaat mooy dëggu?",
  "Download": "Wàcce",
  "Draft status": "Statusu Brouyon",
  "EU AI Act: What Actually Applies on 2 August 2026": "EU AI Act: What Actually Applies on 2 August 2026",
  "Educational demo: HMAC-SHA256 with a shared secret, showing request-bound, expiring, verifiable license tokens. Production tokens should be signed asymmetrically, with the publisher’s public key discoverable under /.well-known/.": "Misaal-njàngale: HMAC-SHA256 ak benn kaw-kaw bu ñu bokk, wone token yu lisaans yu jokkoo ci laaj bi, yu am jamono bu jeex, te ñu man a wóolu. Token yu prodiksion war nañu leen signé ci anam bu asimetrik, ak coppite bu askan bu ki génne content jël, ñu man koo gis ci suuf /.well-known/.",
  "Eight more /topics entries, this time researched by an AI agent rather than curated by hand — same rule as before: every source fetched and confirmed live, summaries an original paraphrase, before anything gets added. 14 entries total.": "Juróom-ñeenti dugub yu bees ci /topics, léegi ku leen njàngat mooy agent AI, du ñu leen bind ci loxo. Menn yoon a nekk: gëblag gu nekk ñu ko jël te wóolu ne mu am tay-tay, dooleel yi ay paraphrase orijinal, laata dara dugal. 14 dugub lépp.",
  "Email": "Imel",
  "Emotion Concepts and Their Function in a Large Language Model": "Emotion Concepts and Their Function in a Large Language Model",
  "Empirical Research": "Njàngat Empirik",
  "English edition →": "Edisioŋ Angale →",
  "Ensure openness is machine-executable — so goodwill is not discarded as legal uncertainty.": "Wóolu ne ubbeeku bi masin man na koy doxal — ngir yërmande wuñu koy sànni ni njàŋat-jàŋat ci wàllu sart.",
  "Epistemology": "Epistemoloji",
